    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Kate Bush’s Best of The Other Sides, released in 2025, is a curated compilation of B-sides and previously unreleased tracks, offering a concise overview of the more experimental and lesser-known corners of her catalog. The album features remastered versions of standout tracks such as “Experiment IV,” “You Want Alchemy?,” and “Walk Straight Down the Middle,” each updated with subtle edits and improved EQ to enhance their sonic clarity. Musically, the collection spans electronic, rock, and pop styles, showcasing Bush’s signature blend of atmospheric production, inventive arrangements, and lyrical depth. The inclusion of her cover of Elton John’s “Rocket Man” further highlights her versatility and interpretive skill.\n\nAs a companion to the 2019 box set The Other Sides, this release distills the essence of Bush’s non-album material, making it accessible to fans who missed the original box set. The album was released digitally on September 26, 2025, with physical editions following on October 31, 2025, on her own Fish People label. Best of The Other Sides reached number 16 on the UK Albums Download Charts and received strong critical praise, with outlets like Classic Pop awarding it a 9/10 and Rolling Stone noting the enduring relevance and quality of the tracks. The release reaffirms Bush’s reputation for artistic innovation and cements the importance of these “other” tracks within her broader discography.",
